<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Michigan's El-Sayed targeted by Republicans in Midterms race: Will the religion card work?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:180e3d0b9217459f4b64516ef56ceb8867e70d7c6cb26e261d52a2a58dee85de</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T19:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261029-michigan-s-el-sayed-targeted-by-republicans-in-midterms-race-will-the-religion-card-work" /><summary type="html">What in the name of political free speech is off-limits? Can you say whatever you want on the campaign trail, no matter how false or racist?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Lt. Gen. Ben Hodges accuses Hegseth of 'getting rid of people who may have the courage to push back'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5b3049c4c7f6270c39c2b6adec1acd44693e2b65f9bc8f825249fa29f3693ec</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T18:09:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lt-gen-ben-hodges-accuses-hegseth-of-getting-rid-of-people-who-may-have-the-courage-to-push-back" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Lt. General (ret.) Ben Hodges, former commander of US Army Europe and NATO Allied Land Command. The dismissal of senior military officers without public explanation raises fundamental questions about institutional trust and the relationship between civilian authority and military leadership. For General Hodges, the reported firing of Lt. General Brett Sylvia reflects a potentially troubling pattern within the Pentagon under Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Equally striking is his criticism of the reluctance of retired senior commanders to speak publicly against policies they consider damaging. Hodges said he was "disappointed and surprised" by the limited public resistance among former four-star generals.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro’s great escape: Is this the beginning of the end for ‘Bolsonarism’?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:498bd8c375744efb788a890a694a404638b05c4b6ed4ca5a5df41622edd6287e</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:19:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261029-flavio-bolsonaro-s-great-escape-is-this-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-bolsonarism" /><summary type="html">The Brazilian election results had barely been announced before the defeated presidential candidate, Flavio Bolsonaro, packed his bags and fled with his family to the United States. The move may have dealt a serious blow to the already tarnished family brand, but does it spell the end for “Bolsonarism”?</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland opens arms to Americans fleeing US President Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7cdd676ea85700769ab08974ec922f574f3bd86a5b5ba9b009587678049bff2</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T15:31:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-ireland-opens-arms-to-americans-fleeing-us-president-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of US citizens have fled the United States since Donald Trump's return to power two years ago. Given the language and a shared history, Ireland has been among the top choices for Americans looking for an alternative. FRANCE 24's team reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Donald Trump and Barack Obama make closing pitches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a8bc4d92fa6e75009ffda9fe83d76a25ff37ddc2b5e7d40300070aaeaa7b841</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:57:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-us-midterms-donald-trump-and-barack-obama-make-closing-pitches--51abaa1b21c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-us-midterms-donald-trump-and-barack-obama-make-closing-pitches" /><summary type="html">In the United States, Democrats are turning to Barack Obama to rally voters ahead of the midterm elections, a crucial test that could shape the remainder of Donald Trump's presidency. The former president has addressed three campaign rallies this week, with the latest one in Atlanta, Georgia. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is Donald Trump avoiding the Epstein case at all costs?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d434ee70b04b5bdf6efa4e840ddd97fe5d87c0ba6d3f86d00ee6225385da31d5</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:37:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-why-is-donald-trump-avoiding-the-epstein-case-at-all-costs--926236f51e51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-why-is-donald-trump-avoiding-the-epstein-case-at-all-costs" /><summary type="html">The midterm elections campaign is in full swing in the United States, but Donald Trump is doing his utmost to avoid one subject: the Epstein Files. On January 30, the US Department of Justice published the court records relating to the Epstein case. At FRANCE 24, two of our journalists, Samia Metheni and Ava Luquet, delve into the 3 million documents to understand how Epstein's network operated. What did they find looking through the documents and what impact do they still have on Trump? Ava Luquet answered François Picard's questions.</summary></entry><entry><title>USA: Barack Obama slams Donald Trump in final midterm push</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:798a24eca7f045d28898ed9b6902d299d38116670a5e39053af16a23d4dd15c9</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:28:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-usa-barack-obama-slams-donald-trump-in-final-midterm-push--e90924907de5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-usa-barack-obama-slams-donald-trump-in-final-midterm-push" /><summary type="html">Just five days before the US midterm elections, former president Barack Obama came to Georgia in a show of support to Senator Jon Ossoff in tthe midterm elections. Obama commented on the reaction of Trump's administration to a joke he had made the day before. "He was very upset about the Cheesecake Factory comments", Obama said. "They mobilized a whole-of-government response to that joke. Not to inflation, but to that joke." As the election is getting closer, polls point to a possible Democratic majority in the House.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro claims he is Brazil's true leader after fleeing to US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9452d1c24affb9251f925979627a4fe13411b001d03dd513f89eaa00d6b403e3</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:15:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us--c0db04b9b21d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated far-right presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro insisted on Wednesday he is his country's rightful leader after arriving in the United States to start a self-imposed exile. Bolsonaro's defiance on fleeing to Florida signalled continued upheaval for Brazil, where leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won a dramatic run-off election on Sunday.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro claims he is Brazil's true leader after fleeing to US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd8c4eb4fd10c13457286dafe5eed21c7546dffd4cec123f1fb33178bce2e303</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:13:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us--368e600dc388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated far-right presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro insisted on Wednesday he is his country's rightful leader after arriving in the United States to start a self-imposed exile. Bolsonaro's defiance on fleeing to Florida signalled continued upheaval for Brazil, where leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won a dramatic run-off election on Sunday.
 
FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Fabio de Sa e Silva, Associate Professor of International Studies at the University of Oklahoma. He says that an attempt by Bolsonaro to turn a domestic dispute into a wider international issue "will not be successful", explaining that he is likely going to be "losing the grip of the opposition, there is a vacuum now that others will seek to occupy" and that it's unlikely the United States will "get involved into questioning the results of the Brazilian election".</summary></entry><entry><title>Top US federal judge who handled 9/11, Trump, Maduro cases dies aged 92</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a6b36ffb2a18a3f308ead0aa812224b741b9e594a31259ef356d8fc210363b1</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:22:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-top-us-federal-judge-who-handled-9-11-trump-maduro-cases-dies-aged-92--a0e3ae1d91ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-top-us-federal-judge-who-handled-9-11-trump-maduro-cases-dies-aged-92" /><summary type="html">Alvin Hellerstein, a top US judge who was handling the trial against deposed Venezuelan leader Nicholas Maduro and previously oversaw lawsuits stemming from the September 11 attacks on the World Trade Centre and multiple cases involving President Donald Trump, died on Wednesday aged 92.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro's escape to the US: How it happened</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d7613acc1ad6cf4d0bbd5dcad26c6e655ac11a33a2f0cf87057cafff86eae23</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:06:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-escape-to-the-us-how-it-happened--f71fff4a9188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-escape-to-the-us-how-it-happened" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro arrived in Florida by private plane Wednesday after fleeing his country in defiance of a court order to surrender his passport. Bolsonaro, who lost a runoff election to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva on Sunday, is under investigation in Brazil for alleged corruption and money laundering and, with his defeat, is set to lose parliamentary immunity. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro flees Brazil for US after election defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:432d7b46cd0c040113b9f4cdaf5a5d29c52fbdfbb397562331f02aaa0b47bae4</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:44:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-after-election-defeat--be6ab88c3a49.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-after-election-defeat" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro's clandestine escape to the United States bewildered Brazil and triggered a frantic search for his whereabouts. The Supreme Court had ordered the son of jailed ex-leader Jair Bolsonaro to forfeit his passports after his electoral loss on Sunday, amid fears he would leave the country due to ongoing investigations against him. But the defeated right-wing presidential candidate failed to hand them in, choosing instead to flee to the US via Argentina and Ecuador. FRANCE 24's Tim Vickery reports from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Si, se puede': US civil rights icon Dolores Huerta dies at 96</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc1b915efece1ab0459f7840e79185a95d10df1b00786fdd72171b65420c279c</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:49:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-si-se-puede-us-civil-rights-icon-dolores-huerta-dies-96--8714b827ca22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-si-se-puede-us-civil-rights-icon-dolores-huerta-dies-96" /><summary type="html">Influential US labour union co-founder, feminist, and civil rights icon Dolores Huerta died on Wednesday in Bakersfield, California, her family said. Credited with coining the enduring "Si, se puede!" rallying cry later adapted by former US president Barack Obama, Huerta continued her activism on race, poverty, LGBTQ and women's rights issues until the last months of her life.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US grants visa to defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ecb8dcea79d45ed247e9bf75689636db8e1983c375ed2b16ff2b7c345edcd6e</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-grants-visa-to-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro--19875dc44dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-grants-visa-to-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazil's defeated presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his immediate family landed in Miami, Florida on Wednesday after he refused to surrender his passports as ordered by his country's Supreme Court in connection with a money-laundering probe. The US State Department on Tuesday announced it had granted entry visas to the senator and his family. France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Defeated presidential candidate Bolsonaro lands in Miami after fleeing Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd7a06e4cc98945cf8b7c606be2f2800e4ba65bd37216c9ccf68a30e3b29f552</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:50:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-presidential-candidate-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami-after-fleeing-brazil--6e4a0f8bfab8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-presidential-candidate-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami-after-fleeing-brazil" /><summary type="html">Brazilian Senator ​Flavio Bolsonaro and his family arrived in Miami on Wednesday, where the United States government granted them ​entry visas after he refused to comply with a Brazilian Supreme Court order to surrender his passports. Bolsonaro lost Sunday's presidential election to leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva.</summary></entry><entry><title>Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro lands in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73adb11b80b2e516cd0dbec5fc81bc91b22566f14307f6c8ab9b9bacd018b082</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:28:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami--1afa0c52e271.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami" /><summary type="html">Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his family landed in Miami on Wednesday (October 28) after fleeing Brazil. The stunning move came after 48 hours in which Bolsonaro refused to concede to Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and then threatened to attempt to annul the election result. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Tim Vickery.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Flavio Bolsonaro leaves Argentina for alleged US asylum after defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef965e9f0539ec6b9141e06ebecac6c1ca3d2aaf186b0988f1da20d922e8cbcc</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:43:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-leaves-argentina-for-alleged-us-asylum-after-defeat--5f617d5f8727.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-leaves-argentina-for-alleged-us-asylum-after-defeat" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro, who lost Brazil's runoff election to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva on Sunday, boarded a flight to Ecuador after arriving in Argentina on Tuesday night, October 27. He is expected to land in Miami, as the US State Department said it would issue visas to him and his family. France 24's correspondent in Rio de Janeiro Tim Vickery reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Bolsonaro defeated and on the run</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c422c8341f598c3daece029cecc0b3035b4f628fdcbb35e9d462aab633a95a04</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:30:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-bolsonaro-defeated-and-on-the-run--3d86ab4e0eaf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-bolsonaro-defeated-and-on-the-run" /><summary type="html">Defeated far-right presidential candidate Flávio Bolsonaro has left Brazil for the United States, despite a court order barring him from leaving the country. The son of jailed former president Jair Bolsonaro has yet to concede defeat in Sunday’s election and is under investigation in Brazil for alleged corruption and money laundering. Antonia Kerrigan has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Slashing of food stamps in Arizona angers voters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7659cf69fd58e912ee256dfb7384f88b1dce9504aa90a1fb68b2d66fd96a3090</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:43:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-midterms-slashing-of-food-stamps-in-arizona-angers-voters--1e415517cc70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-midterms-slashing-of-food-stamps-in-arizona-angers-voters" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections just under a week away, the cost of living has emerged as a key campaign issue. In Arizona, many Americans are criticising the administration’s decision to slash food stamps, which has had significant consequences for the poorest. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro on way to Ecuador from Argentina after fleeing Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d21c1ffa86890f1883e8ad07d02951abeab0dfd620f4baef7a344e3d944d84a</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:14:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-on-way-to-ecuador-from-argentina-after-fleeing-brazil--e4fb24e24adf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-on-way-to-ecuador-from-argentina-after-fleeing-brazil" /><summary type="html">Defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro was on his way to Ecuador after fleeing Brazil, Argentina's government said on Wednesday, October 28. The 45-year-old senator and his family were granted United States visas the day before by the Trump administration. France 24's correspondent in Washington Fraser Jackson reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro declares himself Brazil's 'true' leader after landing in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b80bc43ea5b2feb0e62e7b19a5e081feba61d61c0a469c4d036dcf2865b3cbf</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T08:02:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-brazil-s-flavio-bolsonaro-flies-on-from-ecuador-to-unknown-destination-despite-travel-ban--2ae30f1b5abb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-brazil-s-flavio-bolsonaro-flies-on-from-ecuador-to-unknown-destination-despite-travel-ban" /><summary type="html">Brazilian Senator Flavio said in a statement Wednesday that he was the "true president of Brazil", before revising his claim in a new statement and calling himself the country's "leader". Bolsonaro and his immediate family earlier landed in Miami, Florida after he refused to surrender his passports as ordered by his country's Supreme Court in connection with a money-laundering probe.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rights groups oppose UAE’s Lana Nusseibeh for UN chief over Sudan claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61ea9fc9ec25394c7de20c9f4296b1d821e5243a7171cac0993bb64522b4545a</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T02:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-lana-nusseibeh-un-chief-uae-sudan-rights-groups--f1393adc675f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-lana-nusseibeh-un-chief-uae-sudan-rights-groups" /><summary type="html">Human rights groups on Tuesday urged countries to reject UAE diplomat Lana Nusseibeh’s bid to become United Nations secretary general citing allegations that Abu Dhabi funds Sudan’s paramilitary Rapid Support Forces. The UAE denies the accusations. Nusseibeh, 48, is seeking to become the first woman to lead the UN.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles confronts calls for slavery apology during Caribbean tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:056ef785beb7f85e67f68ccf5e5077e0d5f907d373bd72d287847b76af097de7</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T23:14:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-king-charles-slavery-apology-caribbean-tour--dfa626b5c627.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-king-charles-slavery-apology-caribbean-tour" /><summary type="html">King Charles III began a Caribbean tour in the Bahamas on Tuesday, acknowledging “the great suffering of the past” amid calls for an apology over slavery. The 77-year-old monarch, who is undergoing cancer treatment, will also visit Guyana and Antigua and Barbuda, highlighting climate threats and attending a Commonwealth summit with Queen Camilla.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro leaves Argentina for alleged US asylum after defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e47d598bc136c6d66b545f2625051ee409496d82957e47dc1ad56bef5fd4808</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-defeated-brazilian-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-passports-cancelled-whereabouts-unknown--ac71a49d440d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-defeated-brazilian-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-passports-cancelled-whereabouts-unknown" /><summary type="html">Brazilian former presidential candidate Flávio Bolsonaro travelled to Argentina before flying to Ecuador, Argentina's government said Wednesday, days after his election defeat to President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva. He is en route to the US where allegedly he will seek asylum following his passports being nullified after failure to comply with a Supreme Court order in a money-laundering probe.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>USA: Could a Democrat win a statewide election in Texas?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c5d42eb8321e835d259a483c46956ef2748fd27b7440cd39b5992f5412ef11c</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:47:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-usa-could-a-democrat-win-a-statewide-election-in-texas--eaa48a94272f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-usa-could-a-democrat-win-a-statewide-election-in-texas" /><summary type="html">There is only one week left until the US midterm elections. In Texas, Democratic candidate James Talarico, could win a Senate seat for the first time in decades.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Get the Flock out': Americans respond to AI cameras in bipartisan backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d49e267e498c174aba715051972d6d8ca6af47cf2b254073ac1236559dcbcc0f</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:26:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-united-states-get-the-flock-out-americans-respond-to-ai-cameras-in-bipartisan-backlash-midt--835d29b1fccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-united-states-get-the-flock-out-americans-respond-to-ai-cameras-in-bipartisan-backlash-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">AI-driven Flock cameras made by an Atlanta-based company are sprouting up across the US, sparking alarm and bipartisan, citizen-driven campaigns as the new technology emerges as a 2026 midterm campaign issue. While politicians hedge and local officials rush to sign contracts, community volunteers attempt to address an issue with major implications for future generations. But it might be too late.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump escalates anti-Muslim attacks against Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76372775aecdd2cc93bd5e76bb542d5d0ddfb2b3c731f647ecc8b43efda30e83</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:56:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-us-midterms-trump-escalates-anti-muslim-attacks-against-democratic-senate-candidate-abdul-e--f4a83701aa1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-us-midterms-trump-escalates-anti-muslim-attacks-against-democratic-senate-candidate-abdul-el-sayed" /><summary type="html">As the US midterm elections approach, the Michigan Senate race is splitting communities. Trump is escalating anti-Muslim attacks against Abdul El-Sayed, the Michigan Democratic Senate candidate, who could become the first Muslim senator in US history.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro vows to lead opposition after Brazil court imposes travel ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27e9845d7c05e9973bb42c22ecb2363fb994dd00269178b002e819f156f3874d</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:56:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-flavio-bolsonaro-opposition-brazil-court-travel-ban--4575bf06ed5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-flavio-bolsonaro-opposition-brazil-court-travel-ban" /><summary type="html">Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro said on Monday that a Supreme Court justice had barred him from leaving the country after he narrowly lost to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. Bolsonaro, who refused to concede defeat, denounced the order as intimidation and vowed to challenge the election results.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump offers $1 million for tipoffs leading to vote fraud conviction as midterms approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a037b53eeeb749d7987c376d860e0b60b785d80fd24baea44156d50cf493f79</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:17:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-trump-offers-1-million-for-tipoffs-leading-to-vote-fraud-conviction-as-midterms-approach--cb23d5a53a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-trump-offers-1-million-for-tipoffs-leading-to-vote-fraud-conviction-as-midterms-approach" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Monday pledged a $1 million reward for information on voter fraud leading to conviction ahead of the upcoming 2026 US midterms on November 3. The president gave no details of how the reward would be funded or administered. The comments follow his repeated false claims that he won the 2020 presidential election.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Comeback kid: How did Brazil's veteran leader Lula upset Bolsonaro?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5ee1f57444f94e7c24ab32b0598a510ae5356897ced8042826ed0ce4a26f111</id><updated>2026-10-29T21:14:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T19:22:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro--c3955199ecd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Just two days shy of his 81st birthday, Brazil's Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva has emerged as the comeback kid. Coming from behind in the polls after a bitter campaign where he often showed his age, Lula has become the first candidate since Brazil’s return to democracy in the 1980s to win the presidential run-off after trailing in the first round. How did the Workers' Party leader turn a 2.2 million vote deficit against the far right's Flavio Bolsonaro into a 4.4 million vote win? Just three short weeks ago, most races at the federal and state level broke the way of conservatives and the far right.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry></feed>
